{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The program has no `model` block sampling statements and does not condition on any top-level data variable. `x0` is an unprotected context input used only in `generated quantities` to simulate draws and is not part of a protected likelihood interface.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  vector[3] x0;
}

transformed data {
  int<lower=0> M = 3;           // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N = 100;         // Number of observations

  vector[M] z0 = [-1, 3, 0]';
  real gamma0 = 10;               // True intercept
  vector[M] gamma1 = [2, -3, 1]'; // True slopes
  real sigma = 0.5;              // True measurement variability
}

generated quantities {
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix
  array[N] real y;      // Variates

  for (n in 1:N) {
    X[n, 1] = normal_rng(x0[1], 2);
    X[n, 2] = normal_rng(x0[2], 2);
    X[n, 3] = normal_rng(x0[3], 2);
    y[n] = normal_rng(gamma0 + (X[n] - z0') * gamma1, sigma);
  }
}

","data_safe_json":"{"x0":[5.398829132895872,3.3166416330883113,6.795325086526983]}","protected_variables":[]}
